.TH FERROFIN-SERVER 1 "" Ferrofin "Ferrofin Manual"
.SH NAME
ferrofin\-server \- Ferrofin media server
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBferrofin\-server\fR [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-bind\fR] [\fB\-\-port\fR] [\fB\-\-published\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-ffmpeg\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ferrofin is a Rust implementation of the Jellyfin media server. It speaks the same HTTP API, so existing Jellyfin web, mobile and TV clients connect to it unchanged.
.PP
Pointed at a data directory holding a Jellyfin database, it adopts it in place. Adoption is one\-way: Ferrofin copies the original to jellyfin.db.pre\-ferrofin, then migrates it, and the result may not open under Jellyfin again.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Program\-data root directory (overrides `FERROFIN_DATA_DIR`)
.TP
\fB\-\-bind\fR \fI<ADDR>\fR
Address to bind the HTTP listener to (overrides `FERROFIN_BIND_ADDR`)
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fR \fI<PORT>\fR
HTTP port to listen on (overrides `FERROFIN_PORT`)
.TP
\fB\-\-published\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
Publicly reachable base URL advertised to clients (overrides `FERROFIN_PUBLISHED_URL`)
.TP
\fB\-\-ffmpeg\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Explicit path to the `ffmpeg` executable (overrides `FERROFIN_FFMPEG_PATH`)
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Path to an optional `config.toml` bootstrap file.

When omitted, `{data_dir}/config.toml` is consulted if present.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Every setting has a \fBFERROFIN_*\fR environment variable. Flags override the environment, which overrides \fIconfig.toml\fR. The full list is in \fI/usr/share/doc/ferrofin/CONFIG.md\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/etc/ferrofin/config.toml\fR
Configuration read by the packaged systemd unit. It may hold the bootstrap admin password, so it is root:ferrofin, mode 0640.
.TP
\fI/var/lib/ferrofin\fR
Data directory of the packaged service: the database, cache, logs and plugins.
.TP
\fI/lib/systemd/system/ferrofin.service\fR
The systemd unit. The package does not enable or start it.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fI/usr/share/doc/ferrofin/INSTALL.md\fR, \fI/usr/share/doc/ferrofin/UPGRADING.md\fR, https://github.com/mangoleaf/ferrofin
